> > the idea.
>
> When this idea was discussed last time, I asked how to tell man who
> is still working on an item from a man who forgot about an item and
> effectively blocking others. Do you know an answer?

there's no official "locking" of any item, if that's what you mean.
if someone feels like taking on a specific project, they can always
make that clear on the wiki page, of course.

if someone has "claimed" an item but there's been no progress on that
item for quite some time, it's fair for someone else to ask if that
project has been abandoned.

a better idea might be, if someone claims to be taking on a project,
they might want to post to the wiki page on an occasional basis, just
updating others on their progress.  if it's been a long time since
there's been any addition to a supposedly "claimed" page, that's a
good sign that someone has just walked away from it.

without some official locking or allocation scheme, i think that's the
best you're going to get.  and you can always just ask on the mailing
list.  the wiki is not supposed to be a replacement for anything, just
an extension.

